g Osborn ahead.\n\nThe race shifted in mid-September when a leaked recording surfaced of Osborn criticizing Trump voters, drawing attacks from Ricketts and a $1.4 million GOP super PAC ad buy. Most expert raters call the race Likely R, and prediction markets give Ricketts roughly a 70-85 percent chance. Osborn's path depends on winning over split-ticket voters despite the controversy.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -4.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1701, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.215, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2151, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1705, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.217, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -6.0}]}